<title>USA: BankBoston acquires Nantucket bank.</title>
<headline>BankBoston acquires Nantucket bank.</headline>
<dateline>BOSTON 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>BankBoston Corp said Tuesday that it agreed to buy Pacific National Corp for $24.4 million in stock.</p>
<p>Pacific National's operating unit Pacific National Bank of Nantucket, has three offices and $90 million in deposits and is located on the Massachusetts island of Natucket. BankBoston has assets of $64.8 billion and operates in 23 countries.</p>
<p>BankBoston said the deal, which is subject to shareholder and regulatory approval, is expected to close in October.</p>
<p>It said all employees of Pacific National will remain on the company's payroll through a transition period expected to end on May 31, 1998.</p>
